  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#Atom">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="n2310ddb3cbc14762a79ca19ea8edb924b5"/>
    <vann:example>
        :my-atom a po:Atom ;
                po:isContainedBy :my-paragraph .
        </vann:example>
    <vs:term_status rdf:resource="http://purl.org/linked-data/registry#statusStable"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">atom element</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#"/>
    <owl:disjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#Field"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Literal text that is part of the document body.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">
Similarly to `po:Inline`, elements following the 'atom' pattern can only be contained within block or inline elements (and consequently they also cannot be used as root elements of documents). 
It can contain textual content and no other elements.
    </skos:note>
